rase her from existence why well jen  might have kinda sorta broke the most  cardinal rule of time travel actually  the second most cardinal rule of time  travel the first cardinal rule of time  travel is do not go back in time and put  yourself in a situation where your mom  will try to bang you but the second rule  is definitely that you cannot meddle  with time in order to prevent your  friend's death [ __ ] like that is  guaranteed to cause a rift in space and  time but jennifer decides to warn  hawkeye of his impending doom when his  living past self is brought in to  testify in the present day he's brought  before the tva for her crimes against  time facing permanent expulsion from  reality this time it isn't jen that  saves herself with a brilliant defense  what keeps her alive is the fact that so  many reputable heroes come forward to  vouch for her character innumerable  evidence is given that jennifer walter's  contributions to the multiverse as a  lawyer and a super-powered individual  are too important to delete forever and  the tva reluctantly allows her to live  but these heroes weren't wrong she-hulk  really is far too important to lose  especially after winning the most  important case of all 616 versus the  living tribunal in she-hulk volume 2  number 20 it's revealed that jen was  taken off the world by the living  tribunal and forced to make a case to  save the entirety of the comic's 616  timeline apparently the lt was looking  to replace 616 with the newer more  stylish ultimate universe aka the cosmic  equivalent of a hot trophy wife they  wanted to erase that entire corner of  the multiverse but jen managed to  convince them that 616 is charming not  just in spite of but because of its  convoluted history obviously this was an  editorial in joke about marvel comics  and their reboot attempts with the  ultimate universe but it's canon den  really did save the entirety of 616  through her lawyer skills i don't know  about you but this comic story reminds  me a lot of the ending of eternals when  cersei fastos and kingo are captured by  erysham who informs them that he'll be  using their memories to judge humanity  in the same way that their experiences  will have to convince aeroshem to spare  earth j-hulk was similarly forced to  argue for her world's salvation this  might be a little bit of a rogue theory  but what if shield gets involved helping  these three eternals save the mcu from  heirsham's judgment in future movies i  know i know the eternals have the  situation covered but it would be so fun  to see jennifer walter's space attorney  duking it out alongside cersei with the  big red lego in the sky i might be wrong  but be a girl can dream you gotta admit  tying in the comics 616 universe with  the judgment of the mcu would be a  pretty fun way to showcase that despite  the occasional misstep or mistrial  jennifer walters might just be the most  talented lawyer in the multiverse how  could she not be she single-handedly  uncovered the truth about captain  america's sex life and we as a society  can never repay her for that these are  merely but a delicate sprinkling of the  many court cases from the comics that  prove she held is in fact a very good  attorney i want to hear some of your  favorite verdicts in the comments i'm  sure i ran out of time to list all of  her best cases so hit me up below and  let me know which cases you think might  pop up in future she-hulk episodes or  films follow me on instagram and twitter  whitneypuppy follow new rockstar  subscribe to new rockstars for more  analysis of everything you love and  thanks for watching bye  [Music]  you

